# wave-variety.vrs: wave-variety D18. (1) militia-muster-timed, started at the admin, queues wave 2 at its 75 s beat while
# wave 1 still lives: no "wave 1 cleared" line between wave 1 and wave 2 (Chaos is invulnerable and never attacks). (2)
# undead-onslaught, with its final roll set to 2-2 by `.nyar event set`, logs a "rolled:" line per wave naming only undead
# pool units (CHAR_Undead_* and the two allied CHAR_Cultist_*; the regex refuses any other prefab, and allows the
# line's "… and <n> more" cut at the wire size), its middle wave names
# exactly one boss and its final wave two distinct bosses, and both final bosses spawn (the verbose "spawned <prefab> for
# undead-onslaught" line of each). Every run stopped leaves "tracked units: 0". The events made here are deleted at the end.
# Needs: the step 3 Release DLL; [Debug] VerboseLogging = true; NyarDevTools (.devgo) and DevChatEcho; the pond mark; pillar spawns on; no other event
# running; Chaos invulnerable (true only).
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .devgo pond
expect-log \[DEV TP\] pond
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar event delete militia-muster-timed
wait 1
chat .nyar event delete militia-muster-timed confirm
wait 2
chat .nyar event delete undead-onslaught
wait 1
chat .nyar event delete undead-onslaught confirm
wait 2
#
# (1) timed: wave 2 comes on the beat, wave 1 alive
chat .nyar template use militia-muster-timed
expect-reply militia-muster-timed
chat .nyar event enable militia-muster-timed
expect-reply militia-muster-timed
mark
chat .nyar event start militia-muster-timed
expect-log event militia-muster-timed started by timeout=20
expect-log event militia-muster-timed wave 1/5: 6 units queued timeout=30
wait 10
shot full timed-wave1
expect-no-log event militia-muster-timed wave 1 cleared timeout=55
expect-log event militia-muster-timed wave 2/5: 9 units queued timeout=30
wait 5
shot full timed-wave2
chat .nyar event stop militia-muster-timed
expect-log event militia-muster-timed stopped timeout=20
wait 20
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0
#
# (2) onslaught: pools only, one boss mid-run, two distinct bosses at the end
chat .nyar template use undead-onslaught
expect-reply undead-onslaught
chat .nyar event set undead-onslaught action.waveList.3.bosses pool:lords:2-2
expect-reply undead-onslaught action.waveList.3.bosses =
chat .nyar event enable undead-onslaught
expect-reply undead-onslaught
mark
chat .nyar event start undead-onslaught
expect-log event undead-onslaught started by timeout=20
expect-seen event undead-onslaught wave 1/3 rolled: (?:CHAR_(?:Undead|Cultist)_\w+x[0-9]+(?:, )?)+(?: … and [0-9]+ more)?\s*$ timeout=30
expect-no-log event undead-onslaught wave 1/3 rolled: .*; bosses: timeout=1
wait 10
shot full onslaught-wave1
expect-log event undead-onslaught wave 2/3: [0-9]+ units queued timeout=90
expect-seen event undead-onslaught wave 2/3 rolled: (?:CHAR_(?:Undead|Cultist)_\w+x[0-9]+(?:, )?)+(?: … and [0-9]+ more)?; bosses: CHAR_Undead_\w+\s*$ timeout=10
wait 10
shot full onslaught-wave2
expect-log event undead-onslaught wave 3/3: [0-9]+ units queued timeout=90
expect-seen event undead-onslaught wave 3/3 rolled: (?:CHAR_(?:Undead|Cultist)_\w+x[0-9]+(?:, )?)+(?: … and [0-9]+ more)?; bosses: (?P<B1>CHAR_Undead_\w+), (?P<B2>CHAR_Undead_\w+)\s*$ timeout=10
wait 15
expect-seen \[nyar\] spawned ${B1} for undead-onslaught
expect-seen \[nyar\] spawned ${B2} for undead-onslaught
shot full onslaught-bosses
chat .nyar event stop undead-onslaught
expect-log event undead-onslaught stopped timeout=20
wait 25
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0
chat .nyar event delete militia-muster-timed
wait 1
chat .nyar event delete militia-muster-timed confirm
expect-reply militia-muster-timed
chat .nyar event delete undead-onslaught
wait 1
chat .nyar event delete undead-onslaught confirm
expect-reply undead-onslaught
